etadata field is not consistent, set it to null.\n   - Metadata keys:\n       - location\n       - subject_matter\n       - industry\n       - time  (represents WHEN the event occurred, not when published)\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this structure:\n\n{\n  "subject": "...",\n  "predicate": "...",\n  "object": "...",\n  "metadata": {\n    "location": "... or null",\n    "subject_matter": "... or null",\n    "industry": "... or null",\n    "time": "... or null"\n  }\n}\n\nHere are the RawRecords:\n\nID: 4167642\nCREATED: 2026-06-07\nDOMAIN: ocregister.com\nSLUG: multiple-people-shot-near-music-festival-in-toledo\nTEXT: Multiple people were shot near the Old West End Festival in Toledo, Ohio. The victims, described as "many", were transported to nearby hospitals after police responded to a report of a person shot at around 5:30 p.m. on Saturday. Witnesses, including Kevin Berry, who was listening to live music with friends in the neighborhood arboretum, reported hearing a handful of gunshots and seeing at least five people with gunshot wounds. Authorities are still searching for the suspects, but did not provide details on what may have set off the shooting.\n\nID: 4167516\nCREATED: 2026-06-07\nDOMAIN: apnews.com\nSLUG: toledo-ohio-shooting-4fbc465161cf1d4e29f0f1b22d3fb9d3\nTEXT: Multiple people were shot near the Old West End Festival in Toledo, Ohio, on Saturday. Police responded to a report of a person shot at 5:30 p.m. and found multiple shooting victims, who were transported to nearby hospitals. Authorities did not provide details on the injuries or how many people were shot, nor what may have triggered the shooting. Kevin Berry, who was listening to live music with friends in a neighborhood arboretum, heard gunshots and saw a gun being tossed to the ground 15 meters away.\n\n\n',)
